  "Question": "If \\(5\\) times a number is \\(2,\\) then \\(100\\) times the reciprocal of the number is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2.5\\)",
    "B": "\\(40\\)",
    "C": "\\(50\\)",
    "D": "\\(250\\)",
    "E": "\\(500\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(5\\) times the number equals \\(2\\), the number is \\(2\\div5=\\frac25\\). This is nonzero, so its reciprocal exists and is \\(\\frac52\\).\n\nTherefore \\(100\\) times the reciprocal is\n\\[\n100\\times\\frac52=50\\times5=250.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{250}\\), choice D.",
